content:
Since the first evaluation in 1998, KeyRing has consistently received positive reviews of the quality of its service and its cost-effectiveness. A 2018 evaluation by the Housing Learning and Improvement Network concluded that each year the presence of
    the KeyRing networks led to: 30% of members avoiding a psychiatric inpatient admission; 30% fewer cases of homelessness; 25% of members no longer requiring weekly visits from community psychiatric nurses or social workers/care coordinators; 
    and 20% of members no longer requiring weekly drug/substance misuse worker visits.

